        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function sets up the interrupt system such that interrupts caused by Hot-Plug-Detect (HPD) events and pulses are handled. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function is application-specific for systems that have an interrupt controller connected to the processor. The user should modify this function to fit the application.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>InstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>is a pointer to the <ref refid="struct_x_dp_psu" kindref="compound">XDpPsu</ref> instance. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>IntcPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>is a pointer to the interrupt instance. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>IntrId</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>is the unique device ID of the interrupt controller. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>DpIntrId</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>is the interrupt ID of the DisplayPort TX connection to the interrupt controller. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>HpdEventHandler</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>is a pointer to the handler called when an HPD event occurs. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>HpdPulseHandler</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>is a pointer to the handler called when an HPD pulse occurs.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS if the interrupt system was successfully set up.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE otherwise.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>An interrupt controller must be present in the system, connected to the processor and the DisplayPort TX core. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
