    <briefdescription>
<para>Contains a design example using the <ref refid="struct_x_dp_psu" kindref="compound">XDpPsu</ref> driver with interrupts. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Upon Hot- Plug-Detect (HPD - DisplayPort cable is plugged/unplugged or the monitor is turned on/off), the main link will be trained.</para><para><simplesect kind="note"><para>This example requires an interrupt controller connected to the processor and the DisplayPort TX core in the system. </para><simplesectsep/><para>For this example to display output, the user will need to select the Test Pattern Generator or initialize and select an appropriate source. </para><simplesectsep/><para>DpPsu_PlatformInit and the DpPsu_StreamSrc* functions are empty stubs in <ref refid="xdppsu__common__example_8c" kindref="compound">xdppsu_common_example.c</ref> for the user to fill in as needed.</para></simplesect>
<preformatted>
MODIFICATION HISTORY:</preformatted></para><para><preformatted>Ver   Who  Date     Changes
<hruler/>

1.0   aad 09/04/17 Initial creation.
</preformatted> </para>    </detaileddescription>
